==Battleground==
*1 [[Bore]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Croakley]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Bore]] spawns.
**1 [[Boraphim]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
**1 [[Ribbo]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage is very straightforward. Use [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] to stall the Bore at the start and get money in addition to stacking some [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel]]/[[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|Red]] debuffers (such as [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] or [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet the Maiko]]) to deal with the Boraphim and Bore. Take the [[Ototo Corps|Breakerblast Cannon]] to break Ribbo's [[Barrier]]. [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] and [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attackers]] work well here.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Mitama the Oracle]]: Mitama's 80% Slow uptime drastically reduces the pushing power of Boraphim and Bore. She is also immune to Slow, so Croakley is not an issue for her.
*[[One-Eyed Asuka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blue-Eyed Asuka]]: Being immune to Slow, Asukasli can reach the frontline easily and deal consistent DPS. To ensure she performs well, make sure to send her out only when Boraphim and Bore are Slowed or Frozen, as they'd otherwise push into her blindspot rather easily.
*[[Ken (Uber Rare Cat)|Crimson King of Battle Ken]]: Another great support for this stage with Strong, Weaken, and Knockback vs both Angel and Red. Has Slow immunity as well, so Croakley won't render him useless.

==Trivia==
*Since it's in the same sub-chapter as the [[wikipedia:Socrates|Socrates]]-inspired [[Sage of Mind Soractes]], Forest of Irony may refer to [[wikipedia:Socratic irony|Socratic irony]].

